  "query_preview": "..\n(Tomorrow through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1057 AM CDT Wed Jul 22 2026\n\nThe reprieve from heat will continue Thursday with dry conditions\nfor the most part. However a few elevated showers or \nthunderstorms moving across Kansas associated with a weak \ndisturbance may briefly build into areas near the border Thursday\nmorning. By Friday and Saturday, hotter and more humid conditions\nbegin to return courtesy of increasing south winds, but some \nuncertainty remains as a more significant shortwave is expected \nto top the upper ridge with higher confidence in a few showers and\nthunderstorms developing across northeast OK and northwest AR \nFriday into Friday night. As such, cloud cover may temper the \nwarm-up to some degree. At this point confidence in need for heat \nheadlines remains greater across western areas Saturday.\n\nThe heat looks to return in full force Sunday through at least\nearly next week, with triple-digit high temps becoming more \nlikely and heat headlines needed.",
